          "name": "Title",
          "fill": "$lt-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Two modes, and the thread underneath both",
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 24,
          "fontWeight": "600",
          "letterSpacing": -0.4
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "c4peaS",
          "name": "Lede",
          "fill": "$lt-slate",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 840,
          "content": "Altitude says who you are addressing. Mode says what kind of exchange it is — and the two have different latency contracts, different sources of truth, and different things left behind. Showing which one you are in is what keeps a two-second fact from being mistaken for an opinion.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
