        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "pZQeK",
          "name": "Trade",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "h1clg",
              "name": "H",
              "fill": "$lt-ink",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "What the shaders buy, and what they cost",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": -0.2
            },
            {
              "type": "rectangle",
              "id": "inc3X",
              "name": "Rule",
              "fill": "$lt-ink",
              "width": 860,
              "height": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "GMWcn",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "THEY ACTUALLY MOVE",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "w7oMD",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "Every halo above this board is one frame of a three-rhythm animation, chosen by hand. These run — 4.2s against 3.4s against 9s, which is what stops the Undertow ever quite repeating. That property cannot be drawn.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "fQ2Qy",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "THE SDF FINDS THE SHAPE",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Ykkaf",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "@sdf gives the halo the outline of whatever it wraps, so one file serves a row, a card, a group and a circle. The gradient version needed the stops re-tuned for every aspect ratio, and did the corners badly.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "KrsOS",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "THE UNIFORMS ARE THE RUNTIME",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ZIQCi",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "u_volume is getInputVolume. u_held is the angle the orbit stopped at. u_level is where the waterline sits. These are not styling knobs — they are the state, which means design and implementation stop drifting apart.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "pGSS4",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "ONE FILE PER SIGNAL",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "BXXyd",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "undertow.glsl and understop.glsl are the whole specification, and they are the artefact that ships. No token set to keep in sync, no per-scale variants.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ZS04j",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "THE COST · REDUCED MOTION",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "o8m6h",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "A CSS keyframe stops with prefers-reduced-motion for free. A shader must be told: freeze u_time at the mid-breath frame. Understop is nearly there already; Undertow needs the branch written.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "XvGxT",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "THE COST · IT IS A GPU SURFACE",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "h2GMo",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "Text over it stays DOM, so contrast and selection are unaffected — but every haloed row is a live WebGL context on a phone. On a list of eight running sessions that is a battery decision, not an aesthetic one. Cap the count, or render one shared layer behind the group.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
