              "id": "W7v8Ol",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "THE ORB IS MONOCHROME",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "mcP8I",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "It carries what the agent is doing right now — listening, speaking, thinking, connecting — as motion of a point lattice. No hue at all, which is what the design system asks for and what my petal version was quietly spending.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "QQVNX",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "THE HALO KEEPS THE COLOUR",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "SCQol",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "Undertow and Understop stay on the blue axis around it. So one object answers two different questions at once without either signal borrowing the other's vocabulary.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "l2IfJb",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "ONE DARK OBJECT IN A LIGHT APP",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "c8JFXm",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "A point cloud is luminous, which needs a dark ground. That makes the orb the single dark thing on a white screen — which is what the Broomva blackhole mark already is. The comparison row above has it on paper, on ink, and on deep blue so the ground can be chosen rather than assumed.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "xtsuw",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "THE STATES ARE UNIFORMS, NOT ARTWORK",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "DQign",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "standing is spin 0.16 and nothing else. you-talking is u_volume, which drives dot size and brightness rather than deforming the sphere — louder reads as a brighter lattice. walkie-talking is u_wave, a band travelling up. thinking is spin plus a little scatter. connecting is scatter resolving to zero.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "RQ5Cm",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "KNOWN, UNRESOLVED",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "wmNwS",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 860,
              "content": "Two things are not settled. u_scatter — the dissolve used for connecting — reliably blanks the sphere in this renderer at any non-zero value, so connecting is expressed with u_radius instead and the dissolve is parked. And at 44px in the dock a 170-point lattice will very likely turn to mush; the reference ships a 20px variant, so it is solvable, but it is a fork in the shader rather than a scale factor.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
