        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "wAET8",
          "name": "Wiring",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "GCoOn",
              "name": "H",
              "fill": "$lt-ink",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "What each uniform is wired to",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": -0.2
            },
            {
              "type": "rectangle",
              "id": "K3rzj",
              "name": "Rule",
              "fill": "$lt-ink",
              "width": 880,
              "height": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "C1fLPl",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "u_in ← getInputVolume()",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "t0ocDV",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Your voice lifts the whole lattice at once — every point brighter and slightly larger, tinted toward blue. It is an undirected gesture because your speech arrives all at once from outside the sphere.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "rn4lp",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "u_out ← getOutputVolume()",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "rjIol",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Walkie's voice lifts only the band it is travelling through, rising up the sphere on a 2.5s cycle and tinting it ice. Directed, because its speech is being produced from somewhere.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "LGN5s",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "BOTH AT ONCE",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "T624WS",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Full duplex is now a single picture rather than two states: a blue lattice with an ice band moving through it. That is the barge-in case, and it is the one thing the previous two-state orb could not say.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "tQjKb",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "u_work ← the run",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "kNCvB",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "The Undertow, outside the sphere. Pools on 4.2s, tide on 3.4s, orbit on 9s, never quite repeating. It does not react to sound at all, so voice and work never fight for the same edge.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "o3TBP",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "u_paused ← the ask",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ZU1R8",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "The Understop replaces it: the tide finds its level and lays a line straight through, the orbit holds where it stopped. Visible in the last case, and unmistakable next to a running one.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "BQLqn",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "THE DIVISION HOLDS",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "U9uHJv",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Inside the sphere is who is speaking. Outside it is what the work is doing. One object, two questions, and neither borrows the other's vocabulary — which is what the separate halo and orb could never quite guarantee.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "wECgR",
          "name": "Scale finding",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "w6inpD",
              "name": "H",
              "fill": "$lt-ink",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Two things were wrong, and one of them was not taste",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": -0.2
            },
            {
              "type": "rectangle",
              "id": "N8xaxf",
              "name": "Rule",
              "fill": "$lt-ink",
              "width": 880,
              "height": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "H3TIQC",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "THE WHITE SMUDGE WAS A BUG",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "IaEcB",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "The compositing chain already produces premultiplied colour — halo over body over lattice — and then the shader multiplied by alpha a second time. Every soft region got washed toward the background, which is the pale haze that sat between the dots and the blue. One line.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "pol8F",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "THE LATTICE HAS A NATURAL SIZE",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "a7eVgh",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "It reads as texture at roughly 44 to 96 pixels and as a grid of polka dots much above that, whatever the dot size or count. The reference ships 20px and 64px for the same reason. Raising the count to 340 or 520 to compensate hangs the renderer, so that escape is closed.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "A7nz4",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "SO SCALE COMES FROM THE WEATHER",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "UHSDM",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "u_radius 0.26 rather than 0.52: the sphere stays around fifty pixels and the halo takes the rest of the frame. The hero orb is now large because the Undertow is large, not because the lattice was stretched — which is the right hierarchy anyway, since the weather is the part that carries across a room.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "O3zSAy",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "STILL OPEN",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Jnptd",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "At dock size the sphere would be about twelve pixels at this ratio, which is too small to read. Small placements likely want u_radius back near 0.5 with the halo suppressed — one more uniform pairing to settle, not a new shader.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "oA4zZ",
          "name": "Size presets",
