          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "qR4cY",
          "name": "Bleed finding",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "c1qAKD",
              "name": "H",
              "fill": "$lt-ink",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Letting the weather inside, and what it costs",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": -0.2
            },
            {
              "type": "rectangle",
              "id": "s1bUs",
              "name": "Rule",
              "fill": "$lt-ink",
              "width": 880,
              "height": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "x8BDW",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "IT IS THE TRUER STATEMENT",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "V54jT",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "The run is happening inside the machine, not around it. A ring says the work is adjacent to the agent; a pool crossing the lattice says the agent is the thing doing it. Same information, a better sentence.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "b5Cg8",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "IT FORCED A CLEANER SPLIT",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Ic3I4",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Sharing one space meant voice and work could not both own hue — your blue and the run's blue were the same mark, and the fourth case proved it. So voice is now size and brightness, work is colour. That rule is better than the one it replaced and it only surfaced because of this question.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "t6YQTr",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "THE UNDERSTOP GAINS THE MOST",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "J14Yv",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "The waterline stops being a line drawn beside the orb and becomes one plane passing through it, so the inside and the outside are the same plane. On paper especially it now reads as a single continuous object rather than a sphere with a mark near it.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "VxiHL",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "WHAT IT COSTS",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "p4ZyaK",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "The sphere is no longer neutral. With a run bleeding and a voice lifting at the same time the lattice is genuinely busy, and a third simultaneous signal would break it. Whatever comes next has to go outside, or not exist.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "m8zP9T",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "SMALL SIZES KEEP THE OLD RULE",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "n6sdc",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "At dock size the internal weather is a handful of pixels and reads as noise. Below roughly 88px, u_bleed goes to zero and the contained version stands — which the size presets above already assume.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "MDPl7",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "MY CALL",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "EqDWN",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Default it on above 88px. It is semantically better, it improved the channel split, and it is the first version where the orb and the halo look like one object instead of two layers that happen to be concentric.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "uwC3T",
          "name": "Paused rework",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "oouXP",
              "name": "H",
              "fill": "$lt-ink",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Three attempts at paused, and why the good-looking one was wrong",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": -0.2
            },
            {
              "type": "rectangle",
              "id": "IGvo7",
              "name": "Rule",
              "fill": "$lt-tidepool",
              "width": 880,
              "height": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "GeNqx",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "THE HELD ARC HAD TO GO",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "t6Wfi",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "A stopped orbit sounds right and looks like a smear — a diagonal streak leaking off one side that read as a rendering fault, not as stillness. Stillness is better carried by everything else going quiet than by freezing one moving part.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "v2Zo4Y",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "THE FILL LOOKED BEST AND SAID THE WRONG THING",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "xrz4I",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Filling the sphere to a level gave it real mass and was easily the most attractive version. It also draws a half-full vessel, which reads as a progress meter — the one thing this system refuses to show. Dropped on those grounds, not on looks.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "e1f4qR",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "A LATTICE CANNOT DRAW A LINE",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "E74Hwa",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Asking the points to describe the level produced a scatter of cyan dots, because a lattice only has ink where points happen to fall. The surface is now drawn as one continuous mark across the sphere, and the points near it merely tint. That is the version on the board.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "R3dV36",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "WHAT PAUSED IS NOW",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ridvX",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "The lattice hushes to about sixty percent, one level crosses it, and the same level continues softly outside as a wide low band. No motion, no fill, no frozen arc — a surface at rest, which is what the state actually is.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
