        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "A8OLB",
          "name": "Differences",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "X9juCA",
              "name": "H",
              "fill": "$lt-ink",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "What actually changes between the two modes",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": -0.2
            },
            {
              "type": "rectangle",
              "id": "F7quxr",
              "name": "Rule",
              "fill": "$lt-ink",
              "width": 880,
              "height": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Cgtyn",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "u_body 1 → 0",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "IZUWN",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "The one real decision. On a dark ground the sphere needs a body to contain the light. On paper the body is what ruins it — a filled disc with even dots reads as a golf ball. Drop it and the page becomes the sphere; the lattice alone describes the surface, and the rim crowding does the rest.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "YrYwl",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "u_shade 0 → 1",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "i3Acw",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Only matters when a body is present. It gives the sphere a lit side, a shaded side and a hairline, and it steepens the depth falloff so the far side genuinely recedes instead of showing through.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "sQDoz",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "INK, NOT BLACK",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "VKWt7",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Dots are #2A3140, not the full ink. At full strength on near-white the lattice is harsh and mechanical; a step lighter and it reads as graphite pressed into the page.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "f4WI3",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "WALKIE GOES TIDEPOOL",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "W1vvU",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Ice reads on a dark sphere and vanishes on paper, so walkie's voice tints to tidepool in light mode. Yours stays blue in both. Two hues that survive both grounds, which is the constraint that picked them.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "lXcAD",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "THE HALO IS MASKED",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "kCfjs",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Without a body there is nothing to stop the Undertow flooding through the middle of the lattice, so the weather is now explicitly kept outside the sphere radius. Harmless in dark mode, load-bearing in light.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "IuFMS",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "WHAT DID NOT CHANGE",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "d9QsDE",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Every state, every rhythm, and both voice gestures. One file serves both grounds on five uniforms — no second shader, no forked artwork.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "undBr",
          "name": "Occlusion AB",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 18,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "nco0V",
              "name": "Cap",
              "fill": "$lt-slate",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "The one open choice in light mode. Without a body there is nothing to stop the weather glowing through the middle of the lattice; with one, the occlusion is clean but the constellation becomes an object again. Both at hero size, same uniforms otherwise.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
