        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "E1EIKO",
          "name": "Verdict",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "KwEzw",
              "name": "H",
              "fill": "$lt-ink",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Verdict: tidepool, and running gives up cyan",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": -0.2
            },
            {
              "type": "rectangle",
              "id": "QCf5k",
              "name": "Rule",
              "fill": "$lt-tidepool",
              "width": 880,
              "height": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "gc65o",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "TIDEPOOL → CYAN",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "c89td",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "The system already gives cyan to Needs you, and it separates from the run's blue at a glance in both modes. Cyan to white is brighter and reads slightly hot for a state that is a gate rather than a failure — worth keeping as the variant for anywhere the orb has to compete with a busy surface.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "KPO07",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "DRAINED WAS THE INTERESTING FAILURE",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "LhUq2",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Desaturating the run to a grey-blue is the obvious way to say stopped, and it says the wrong stopped: it reads as inactive, finished, switched off. Paused is not dormant — something is waiting on you, and the colour has to keep some pressure.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "XknVX",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "INVERTED WAS TOO CLOSE",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Bsl6c",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Navy with a cyan highlight is legible on its own and nearly indistinguishable from the run in peripheral vision, which is the only vision that matters for an ambient signal.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ID4Pd",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "THE REAL FIX WAS ON THE OTHER SIDE",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "f9Nj5",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "Separation was muddy until running stopped using cyan. On paper its highlight had been tidepool, so the two states were competing for one hue. Running is now blue only — blue to ice in dark, blue to blue-ink on paper — and cyan belongs to paused alone.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "qhcvl",
              "name": "K",
              "fill": "$lt-mist",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "WHAT THIS COSTS",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "kmidZ",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 880,
              "content": "In light mode walkie's voice tint moves from cyan to blue-ink, so the two voices are closer in hue there. Acceptable, because voice is carried by size and brightness while work owns colour — but it does mean hue can no longer be used to tell you from walkie on paper.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
