          "content": "Fifty screens, one spine, both themes. A native Swift client on your own tailnet, talking to Genesis on the host beside the sessions. The orb is present on every surface — collapsed in the dock or filling the stage — and answers two questions at once: the lattice inside says who is speaking, the weather outside says what the work is doing. Everything else is navigation between three places, plus the rooms you visit once.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ZIuER",
          "name": "H",
          "fill": "$lt-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The spine",
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 17,
          "fontWeight": "600",
          "letterSpacing": -0.2
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "PRsmL",
          "name": "R",
          "fill": "$lt-ink",
          "width": 1064,
          "height": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "KcnH3",
          "name": "K",
          "fill": "$lt-mist",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "HOME  ⇄  VOICE  ⇄  THREAD",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "SWpz9",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Home is the bench: what wants you, what is running, what is standing. Pull the orb up and you are in Voice at whatever altitude the chip says. One tap from Voice is the Thread, which is the record the call has been writing the whole time. Those three cover the entire ordinary day; everything else is entered from them or from a push.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "pgrjS",
          "name": "K",
          "fill": "$lt-mist",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "THE GESTURES",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "UWRBa",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Hold anywhere on the stage to talk · release to send · slide up to cancel · tap the chip to change who you are addressing · pull the dock up to open the call · tap Show thread to drop out of voice without losing the exchange · swipe down to collapse back to the bench.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "GJpaU",
          "name": "H",
          "fill": "$lt-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Entry points",
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 17,
          "fontWeight": "600",
          "letterSpacing": -0.2
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "m8uyKA",
          "name": "R",
          "fill": "$glow-blue",
          "width": 1064,
          "height": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "AVaFg",
          "name": "K",
          "fill": "$lt-mist",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "COLD START — Pair → Microphone → Home",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ze97k",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Two products, once: Tailscale, then the host command. walkie cannot join a tailnet on its own, so first run is a two-step and the second step only lights up when the first has. The allowlist starts empty on purpose. Microphone asks once and says plainly that hold-to-talk keeps the mic closed between turns.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "c0T4L2",
          "name": "K",
          "fill": "$lt-mist",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "A PUSH — Push → Ask",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "RRk9X",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "The only path that skips the bench. The notification states the options count, that evidence is attached, and that voice will not answer this one. It deep-links to Ask, never into a call.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "YL69V",
          "name": "K",
          "fill": "$lt-mist",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "A ROUTINE — Standing → Routine",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Gtr4R",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Set by saying it, never by a form. The list shows why each one last woke; the detail is a wake log, not a settings page.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "dKHQp",
          "name": "H",
          "fill": "$lt-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "What each screen is for",
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 17,
          "fontWeight": "600",
          "letterSpacing": -0.2
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "CfESa",
          "name": "R",
          "fill": "$lt-tidepool",
          "width": 1064,
          "height": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "m7BcsW",
          "name": "K",
          "fill": "$lt-mist",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "ENTRY  ·  row 1",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "I3MwFP",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Pair (Tailscale, then the host) · Microphone · Connecting (four real steps, not a spinner) · Host offline (you are on the tailnet, Genesis is not answering) · Off tailnet (the host may be fine — this is the phone's side) · Empty (nothing reachable yet)",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Qlsbc",
          "name": "K",
          "fill": "$lt-mist",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "BENCH  ·  row 2",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "OYAK5",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Home (needs you, running, standing) · Home all quiet (the good day) · Switcher (who you are addressing, and what that costs) · Standing (routines and their last wake) · Routine (the wake log)",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Xe7ND",
          "name": "K",
          "fill": "$lt-mist",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "VOICE  ·  rows 3 and 4",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "jjxEb",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "orchestrator (thinking with you) · store answered (a fact, 41ms, nothing woken) · escalated (judgement engaged, the sessions gather) · session idle (one altitude down) · you talking · walkie talking · barge-in (both at once) · degraded (audio poor, call intact) · re-established (the 60-minute cap, handled early)",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "P8QYmv",
          "name": "K",
          "fill": "$lt-mist",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "WORK  ·  row 5",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "w9UbkJ",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Session (one workspace) · Look contained (voice may approve, containment proven) · Look needs a screen (voice may only open it) · Look approved · Look sent back · Ask low stakes (the everyday one, answerable out loud) · Ask consequential (the deep link, evidence in mono, no wave capsule) · Ask answered (with an undo window) · Receipts (rung three, opt-in)",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "rFNPu",
          "name": "K",
          "fill": "$lt-mist",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "THREADS AND SYSTEM",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "hBfCs",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Thread orchestrator (with a typed dispatch proposal) · Thread seaslug (direct, with tool receipts) · Dispatch sent · Push · Access (the allowlist, and what voice can never do)",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "nbEr4",
          "name": "H",
          "fill": "$lt-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The rules the screens are obeying",
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 17,
          "fontWeight": "600",
          "letterSpacing": -0.2
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "b6ENX",
          "name": "R",
          "fill": "$lt-amber",
          "width": 1064,
          "height": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "AnYs4",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Running wears the Undertow, paused wears the same weather in cyan, and nothing else moves. Colour belongs to work; size and brightness belong to voice. Needing you is a gate, not a failure — it is never red. Approving is the one human verb, and it happens by voice only where containment is machine-proven. The thread is the audit artifact that voice was missing, which is what lets walkie be used for thinking and not only for triage.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "aP3j1",
          "name": "Where it runs",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 10,
          "padding": [
            0,
            0,
            56,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "snrw0",
              "name": "H",
              "fill": "$lt-ink",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Where it runs",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": -0.2
            },
            {
              "type": "rectangle",
              "id": "MDTlQ",
              "name": "R",
              "fill": "$glow-blue",
              "width": 1064,
              "height": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "zuicf",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$lt-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1064,
              "content": "Phone and host meet on the tailnet; both reach OpenAI over the internet independently. There is no cloud half — a host-resident Genesis satisfies same-UID trust by construction, which is the only thing the old split existed to arrange. The costs are named on the topology board: the host becomes a single point, onboarding gains a dependency, and off-tailnet is a failure mode that needs its own words because the remedy is on the phone rather than the workstation.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "amh6y",
          "name": "Turn-taking",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 10,
          "padding": [
            0,
            0,
            56,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ZS3fq",
              "name": "H",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Turn-taking, decided",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": -0.2
            },
            {
              "type": "rectangle",
              "id": "O2DUu",
              "name": "R",
              "fill": "$tidepool",
              "width": 1064,
              "height": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "brvWX",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$text-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1064,
              "content": "Hold to talk is the default. The product is named after the gesture, the mic stays closed between turns, and earshot being the authentication boundary is a much smaller surface when the mic is shut. Open mic remains available per session — wiring WebRTC directly rather than adopting PushToTalk kept full duplex, so this is a preference rather than a one-way door. Barge-in works in both: under the default you press to cut in, and the overlap while walkie's audio ducks out is real rather than a hard switch, which is why the orb shows both voices during it.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "Xp9GN",
          "name": "Theming",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 10,
          "padding": [
            0,
            0,
            56,
            0
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "nQ0GJ",
              "name": "H",
              "fill": "$text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Both themes, from one set of screens",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 17,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": -0.2
            },
            {
              "type": "rectangle",
              "id": "h867AN",
              "name": "R",
              "fill": "$glow-blue",
              "width": 1064,
              "height": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "LwGWf",
              "name": "V",
              "fill": "$text-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1064,
              "content": "Nothing is drawn twice. Every screen and every shared component points at themed tokens, so switching the mode axis repaints all thirty-four. The orb goes with them: u_sphere, u_ink, u_agent, u_body and u_shade are variables rather than constants, which means the sphere inverts on its own — bodiless ink on paper, a filled luminous lattice on dark. The one rule that survives both is the size split: below 88px the orb keeps a body in either theme, because a bodiless constellation at dock scale is dust.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "zvcAL",
          "name": "H",
          "fill": "$text-primary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The rooms you visit once",
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 17,
          "fontWeight": "600",
          "letterSpacing": -0.2
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "x0ZEz",
          "name": "R",
          "fill": "$amber-t",
          "width": 1064,
          "height": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Grz9z",
          "name": "K",
          "fill": "$text-faint",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "ONBOARDING",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "iwYq5",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "welcome · scope explainer (what voice will and will not do, said before you rely on it) · pair · microphone · microphone denied · notifications · add workspace · ready",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "oe1mI",
          "name": "K",
          "fill": "$text-faint",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "SETTINGS",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Psdi9",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "settings root · turn-taking (the decided fork, exposed) · voice and readback · notifications · appearance (theme, reduced motion, orb density) · diagnostics (link, this call, store, build)",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "dYiiq",
          "name": "K",
          "fill": "$text-faint",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "INSTANCES",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "pVuxc",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "workspaces · workspace detail · orchestrator scope · history",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "e97a62",
          "name": "K",
          "fill": "$text-faint",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "THE ONE ABSENCE",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "RChqf",
          "name": "V",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "There is no page for the orchestrator's instructions, personality or schedule. It is an agent, not a preference: what it should do is something you tell it, and the wake log shows what it did. Its scope screen exists because reachability is a security surface — the rest would be a settings page for something that should have been told.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "P2VM0",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 30400,
      "name": "The ambient layer",
      "width": 1160,
      "fill": "$lt-canvas",
      "cornerRadius": 24,
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 24,
      "padding": [
        48,
        48,
        80,
        48
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "CsbRa",
          "name": "Title",
          "fill": "$lt-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "How far the signal reduces",
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 28,
          "fontWeight": "600",
          "letterSpacing": -0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "alcho",
          "name": "Lede",
          "fill": "$lt-slate",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 880,
          "content": "A Live Activity cannot run a shader — it is a constrained view on a slow update budget. So before drawing any ambient surface, the question is how small the Undertow can get and still say running rather than decorative. It survives three steps down and then becomes a different mark entirely.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "M6K1o",
          "name": "Ladder",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "gap": 36,
          "alignItems": "end",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "PSEbz",
              "name": "200px · stage",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 14,
              "alignItems": "center",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "JRfhp",
                  "name": "Box",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 200,
                  "justifyContent": "center",
                  "alignItems": "center",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "ZutCC",
                      "name": "Orb",
                      "clip": true,
                      "width": 200,
                      "height": 200,
                      "fill": {
                        "type": "shader",
                        "enabled": true,
                        "url": "orb.glsl",
                        "uniforms": {
                          "u_sphere": "#FBFCFD",
                          "u_ink": "#2A3140",
                          "u_you": "#3783F0",
                          "u_agent": "#436EB4",
                          "u_shade": 1,
                          "u_body": 0,
                          "u_bleed": 1,
                          "u_paused_col": "#009BD8",
                          "u_paused_hi": "#5ED3EE",
                          "u_in": 0,
                          "u_out": 0,
                          "u_radius": 0.28,
                          "u_spin": 0.2,
                          "u_work": 1,
                          "u_paused": 0
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  ]
