    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "K9PZ3",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 32200,
      "name": "Topology · Swift + Tailscale",
      "width": 1160,
      "fill": "$lt-canvas",
      "cornerRadius": 24,
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 22,
      "padding": [
        48,
        48,
        72,
        48
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "GUv75",
          "name": "Title",
          "fill": "$lt-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Three legs, one tailnet",
          "lineHeight": 1.2,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 28,
          "fontWeight": "600",
          "letterSpacing": -0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "EPHft",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-slate",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 900,
          "content": "The phone is native Swift and joins the tailnet. Genesis runs on the host beside the sessions it reaches. There is no cloud half any more — the thing that made the deployment split structural was a Railway container being unable to satisfy same-UID trust, and a host-resident service satisfies it by construction.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "mgXmu",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-mist",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "THE LEGS",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "h0BXRv",
          "name": "R",
          "fill": "$lt-ink",
          "width": 1064,
          "height": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "R528U",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-slate",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "phone ⇄ host   ·   over Tailscale",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "s0b3Y",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Everything that is walkie's own traffic. A WebSocket at /ws carries session state and turn events; the ask log, the ephemeral-secret request, the call-id relay and typed dispatches ride the same Hono surface. Nothing is exposed inbound — the tailnet is the authentication boundary, which is a stronger statement than the bearer check it replaces.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "l1oRm",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-slate",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "phone ⇄ OpenAI   ·   over the internet",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "d3LIo",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "The WebRTC media path only. The client still does its own SDP exchange with the ephemeral key, exactly as before. This leg does not touch the tailnet and does not need the host to be reachable once it is up.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "HMK1o",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-slate",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "host ⇄ OpenAI   ·   over the internet",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "a1gkH",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "The sideband, with the standard API key, plus the tool calls Genesis answers. Same as the decided design; it simply lives on the workstation now instead of in Railway.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "QcV0m",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-slate",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "host → APNs → phone",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "SzesA",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Push is outbound from the host, so it works without any inbound exposure and without a cloud relay. It is also the one leg that does not care whether the phone is on the tailnet.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "SrWO3",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-mist",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "WHAT THIS RETIRES",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "B5rW8",
          "name": "R",
          "fill": "$glow-blue",
          "width": 1064,
          "height": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "cjo6z",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "The cloud half, and with it the fan-out service, the artifact server, and the outbound-only Tailscale hop from host to Railway. The doc calls treating these as one deployable “the mistake that makes the whole thing undeployable” — that was true of a Railway container. It is not true of a host-resident Genesis, and the paragraph needs rewriting rather than reinterpreting.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "JgvjU",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-mist",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "WHAT IT COSTS",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "y6dEMo",
          "name": "R",
          "fill": "$lt-amber",
          "width": 1064,
          "height": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ETWDs",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "The host becomes the single point. With a cloud half, an ask could be queued and pushed while the workstation slept; now a sleeping host means no asks reach you at all. That is a real availability regression and it should be a stated product decision, not a discovery.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "pfmxW",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Onboarding gains a dependency. The phone cannot silently join a tailnet — Tailscale is a separate app the user installs and signs into before walkie can reach anything. First run is now two products, not one.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "p0kMd",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "A new failure mode that is not host-offline. Off-tailnet means the host may be perfectly healthy and simply unreachable; the remedy is on the phone, not the workstation, so it needs its own screen and its own words.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "icc3X",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-mist",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "WHAT IT IMPROVES",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "Zs998",
          "name": "R",
          "fill": "$lt-green",
          "width": 1064,
          "height": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "klddM",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Same-UID trust stops being a design problem and becomes a property of where the code runs. The unix socket under /tmp/cc-socks/ is reachable because Genesis is on the same machine as the sessions, which is what the whole host-agent indirection existed to arrange.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Bxa2X",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$lt-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Full duplex stays available. Wiring WebRTC directly with a plain audio session — rather than adopting the PushToTalk framework — keeps both turn-taking modes on the table, so the open-mic question stays open instead of being foreclosed by the client choice.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
