          "fontSize": 28,
          "fontWeight": "600",
          "letterSpacing": -0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "VXvM8",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 900,
          "content": "Read out of apps/genesis rather than assumed. Where the design invented a name, this is the name. Where walkie adds a concept Genesis does not have, that is stated as ours to build rather than left looking like something we can call.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 15,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "xsjPX",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-faint",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "THE PHASE MACHINE — packages/projection/src/reducer.ts",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "nlx8D",
          "name": "R",
          "fill": "$glow-blue",
          "width": 1064,
          "height": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "t4WwfT",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "RunPhase = \"idle\" | \"running\" | \"awaiting\" | \"blocked\" | \"done\"",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "HewPP",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "walkie's plain-voice states map onto it, but not one to one. Running is running. Needs you is awaiting. Stuck is blocked. Done is done. Queued has no Genesis phase — idle is a thread that has never run, which is not the same thing. Standing has none at all: a routine is walkie's, and nothing in the reducer knows about cadence.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "D7xMF",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "The important one: awaiting is entered when the agent calls AskUserQuestion, and the reducer captures pendingQuestion off that tool call. So a walkie ask is not a message we parse — it is a tool invocation with a schema, and its named options are the tool's options. The claim that an ask is structured data and never free text is therefore already true in the engine, not a rule walkie has to impose.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "HngDY",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "done and blocked are absorbing. awaiting survives a turn-ending result, which is why a run can sit waiting on you with no process running.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "W8LvMI",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-faint",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "THE SURFACE — apps/api/src/server.ts, Hono",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "DR5V5",
          "name": "R",
          "fill": "$tidepool",
          "width": 1064,
          "height": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "zb4zX",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "GET /workspaces · POST /workspaces · DELETE /workspaces/:id · GET /workspaces/available · GET /workspaces/browse · POST /workspaces/refresh",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "COuVu",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "GET /workspaces/:id/git/status · /git/diff · POST /git/commit · GET /workspaces/:id/checks · /files · /file",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "dNiri",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "GET /threads · GET /threads/:id · POST /message · POST /control · GET /health",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "kM7AU",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "POST /control takes an action of reset · interrupt · status · archive · unarchive · rename. walkie's Interrupt is that interrupt. walkie's Send back is a POST /message on the thread. walkie's Approve has no counterpart — there is no gate in Genesis, so the gate is ours to define and ours to enforce.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "iaQDD",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-faint",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "TRANSPORT — corrected",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "S1npE",
          "name": "R",
          "fill": "$amber-t",
          "width": 1064,
          "height": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "lJWah",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "It is a WebSocket at /ws?thread=<id>, not SSE. The topology board said SSE for the ask log and session state; that was assumed and is now fixed. Genesis upgrades with createBunWebSocket and the PWA connects per thread — walkie either does the same or adds a fan-out of its own, but it cannot describe what exists today as SSE.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "J5i1oV",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-faint",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "THE WORKSPACE RECORD — packages/core/src/types.ts",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "E3nIM",
          "name": "R",
          "fill": "$glow-blue",
          "width": 1064,
          "height": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "M6bnx9",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Workspace { id, name, rootPath, isGitRepo?, noWorktree?, confined?, home? }",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "O3Oy7",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Session { id, workspaceId, threadId, agentSessionId?, phase, engine?, noWorktree?, branch?, title?, archived? }",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "v2xFI",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "Branches are genesis/<key> for a worktree session, or the repo's current branch when the session runs at the root. The design had invented run/<key>; that is now corrected everywhere it appeared.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "AUUoq",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "noWorktree is a posture, not a constant. It is a workspace default that a session binds stickily on its first turn, so “worktree per run” is true of some sessions and false of others — a nested monorepo runs at the root by design.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "T1o0P",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "confined is the real security flag and walkie's screens now surface it. True means the spawn drops every inherited MCP server; false means the session carries the operator's MCP servers, Gmail, Drive and Calendar connectors. MCP runs outside the filesystem sandbox, so nothing about path confinement touches it.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "QcI1W",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-faint",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "WHAT WALKIE ADDS THAT GENESIS DOES NOT HAVE",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal",
          "letterSpacing": 0.5
        },
        {
          "type": "rectangle",
          "id": "x25bI",
          "name": "R",
          "fill": "$green-t",
          "width": 1064,
          "height": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "RhK8z",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "The voice reachability allowlist. The gate and the approve verb. Standing routines and their cadence. The ask log as an append-only per-user store with acknowledgement. Containment proof for voice approval. The orchestrator plane. None of these exist in Genesis today — every one is a thing to build, and the screens that show them are specifications rather than integrations.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "eSFdV",
          "name": "T",
          "fill": "$text-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1064,
          "content": "There is already a voice channel in Genesis (apps/api/src/voice.ts, BRO-2228) but it is a different product: an ElevenLabs phone agent with voice for intake and WhatsApp for delivery. Its principle is worth inheriting though, and it is the same one the runtime board argues for — nothing in that handler runs an agent; every path answers from state already held or enqueues and returns.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
